---
import Sheet from '../layouts/Sheet.astro';
import Specimen from '../components/Specimen.astro';
import { examples } from '../data/examples';
---

<Sheet
  title="Examples"
  description="Seven bonsai trees grown by node-bonsai, each with the command that makes it."
>
  <h1>Trees to copy</h1>
  <p>
    Each tree below was grown by the real program, and the command under it is what you type to
    get one like it. Change any option and you get a different tree.
  </p>
  <p class="size-note">
    Every tree here is drawn at 80 columns by 24 rows. The shape of a tree also depends on the
    size of your terminal, so the same seed in a bigger or smaller window grows a different tree.
    To get exactly the tree you see here, use the second command under it, which prints at
    80 by 24 whatever your window size is.
  </p>

  <div class="trees">
    {examples.map((example, index) => <Specimen example={example} index={index} />)}
  </div>
</Sheet>

<style>
  .trees { margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
</style>
